            {
                "entry_id": "b0157d5a-b5e5-32a6-9309-236dc0e972cf",
                "word": "Matamore",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6dd23b25-083e-3f1e-acec-b1eee9b602f3",
                        "entry_id": "b0157d5a-b5e5-32a6-9309-236dc0e972cf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Un des personnages de la commedia dell’arte"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "da41fcd3-a49d-4f61-a48e-18141f344f69",
                                "sense_id": "6dd23b25-083e-3f1e-acec-b1eee9b602f3",
                                "text": "J’ai pour théâtre l’univers, et, sans bouger, de mon fauteuil, je suis la comédie ; j’applaudis Matamore ou bien Francatrippa ; je jouis des tournois et des pompes royales, je crie bis à ces gens qui se cassent la tête."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d0c55ca-254b-4249-bb57-140dfa3d2d92",
                                "sense_id": "6dd23b25-083e-3f1e-acec-b1eee9b602f3",
                                "text": "C'est pour celui-ci que fut écrit le rôle de Matamore dans L'Illusion Comique. On peut penser que la pièce avait été commandée par Mondory, comme Le Railleur de Mareschal, qui fut créé avant le carnaval de 1635."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
                        "linkage_id": "1044fb99-4294-4137-9332-c2e90ce5c015",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0157d5a-b5e5-32a6-9309-236dc0e972cf",
                        "source_sense_ids": [
                            "6dd23b25-083e-3f1e-acec-b1eee9b602f3"
                        ],
                        "linkage_type": "synonyms",
                        "word": "Capitan"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "4abc265c-66d1-3b73-b63a-50716104679f",
                "word": "Matamore",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e89bb941-18c0-3cd5-abc1-c99e402b6ebc",
                        "entry_id": "4abc265c-66d1-3b73-b63a-50716104679f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Section de la ville algérienne de Mostaganem."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4832c319-db77-4dc1-9049-0311a3691bdb",
                                "sense_id": "e89bb941-18c0-3cd5-abc1-c99e402b6ebc",
                                "text": "Le territoire de Mostaganem et de Mazagran comprend trois villes distinctes: Mostaganem, Matamore et Mazagran. De ces trois villes, Mostaganem est la plus importante ; Matamore en est en quelque sorte la citadelle."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "caa4f7a4-4971-3379-8fe4-95587a596515",
                "word": "matamore",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c632067c-f28c-4a33-a324-d3d7eaeb744b",
                        "entry_id": "caa4f7a4-4971-3379-8fe4-95587a596515",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "matamores"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2e5f02c0-613f-315f-982b-93da41ad2ed3",
                        "entry_id": "caa4f7a4-4971-3379-8fe4-95587a596515",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Faux brave, vantard plus courageux en paroles qu’en actes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9c1ea39-c664-4d33-80ec-0e4bede25509",
                                "sense_id": "2e5f02c0-613f-315f-982b-93da41ad2ed3",
                                "text": "TOULOUSE – […] Figures et poses involontairement comiques de bravaches et de matamores dans les rues."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "983e44af-f6fb-4e18-a650-c5eb35563aec",
                                "sense_id": "2e5f02c0-613f-315f-982b-93da41ad2ed3",
                                "text": "Peut-être eût-on pu lui reprocher une exubérance de gestes qui n'était pas du meilleur goût, il avait une façon de se camper qui sentait son matamore."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9abd98da-799d-4449-9189-147d061317a1",
                                "sense_id": "2e5f02c0-613f-315f-982b-93da41ad2ed3",
                                "text": "Voilà bien la phobie propre aux Matamores, grands conchieurs de chausses, comme on sait."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be7e81e9-7e02-403b-9ac8-8e1c42e598fb",
                                "sense_id": "2e5f02c0-613f-315f-982b-93da41ad2ed3",
                                "text": "Le boyau était long, l’avance des hommes pénible, Dickson entendait dans son dos haleter ses compagnons, moins aguerris que lui, malgré leurs mines de matamores."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d1153b8-07e2-42ef-9546-61d9be13da8c",
                                "sense_id": "2e5f02c0-613f-315f-982b-93da41ad2ed3",
                                "text": "Sans doute, pour « réparer » Washington, valait-il mieux un ancien sénateur rompu aux arcanes de la politique devenu sur le tard président qu’un matamore populiste."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "15b8c27d-f958-418f-98d8-91a48205cf69",
                        "source_entry_id": "caa4f7a4-4971-3379-8fe4-95587a596515",
                        "source_sense_id": "2e5f02c0-613f-315f-982b-93da41ad2ed3",
                        "target_lang_word": "braggart",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "braggart",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51a5f380-8ed2-363d-a1a6-c1b7b4e7f874",
                                        "entry_id": "d4263855-a5b4-3026-8f30-e680ffd76e90",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who constantly brags or boasts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45ee1c6c-31ca-432b-a027-b58643e30774",
                                                "sense_id": "51a5f380-8ed2-363d-a1a6-c1b7b4e7f874",
                                                "text": "O I could play the woman with mine eyes, / And Braggart with my tongue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c28d36b-c048-4b66-bfc6-354dfea54a86",
                                                "sense_id": "51a5f380-8ed2-363d-a1a6-c1b7b4e7f874",
                                                "text": "Shallow water gives a great splash, and so a braggart has ever been contemptible in my eyes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0252817-6318-4df5-bf66-61e17cd51ecd",
                                                "sense_id": "51a5f380-8ed2-363d-a1a6-c1b7b4e7f874",
                                                "text": "A very good resolve to make and keep, if you would also keep any friends you make, is never to speak of anyone without, in imagination, having them overhear what you say. One often hears the exclamation “I would say it to her face!” At least be very sure that this is true, and not a braggart’s phrase and then—nine times out of ten think better of it and refrain."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "braggart",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "336ff6e6-9f5d-308e-9dcd-607807d12863",
                                        "entry_id": "861e2e01-a1f5-3da6-9ac2-773aa61cf329",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characterized by boasting; boastful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c1db0ef-a178-4608-a7ea-1eb19c556420",
                                                "sense_id": "336ff6e6-9f5d-308e-9dcd-607807d12863",
                                                "text": "O my fair Mistress, Truth! Shall I quit thee, / For huffing, braggart, puft Nobility?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebb6c33c-8136-4fda-81ff-ca2f33315b95",
                                                "sense_id": "336ff6e6-9f5d-308e-9dcd-607807d12863",
                                                "text": "Captain [Benjamin] Bonneville was delighted with the game look of these cavaliers of the mountains, welcomed them heartily to his camp, and ordered a free allowance of grog to regale them, which soon put them in the most braggart spirits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22616bb0-e631-4830-8ad3-c9cdce94b965",
                                                "sense_id": "336ff6e6-9f5d-308e-9dcd-607807d12863",
                                                "text": "He took him on the long walks of which he was fond, and made him in some sort his humble confidant, talking to him of himself and his plans with large and braggart vagueness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0d53f371-47c8-43d4-b934-c03d4a0642b6",
                        "source_entry_id": "caa4f7a4-4971-3379-8fe4-95587a596515",
                        "source_sense_id": "2e5f02c0-613f-315f-982b-93da41ad2ed3",
                        "target_lang_word": "blusterer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
